# Interceptor USV digital-twin ArduRover defaults.
#
# Represents an Indian Navy autonomous fast interceptor boat -- the real
# programme (BEL + WESEE "A2NCS", Advanced Autonomous Navigation & Control
# Software) retrofits autonomy onto an in-service fast interceptor hull
# (~16 m LOA, ~45 kn; Solas Marine class). Published class specs are in
# README.md.
#
# FIDELITY NOTE: the real craft runs A2NCS, not ArduRover. This twin stands it
# up on ArduRover because the range tests the MAVLink/autopilot attack surface;
# the HULL is represented by the CUSV Gazebo body (sim_config/models/cusv --
# the nearest unmanned surface combatant model). Real interceptor hydrodynamics
# (planing monohull, high speed) are documented, not reproduced in the SDF
# (Tier-A body). Command-authentication findings are firmware-accurate.
#
# Stock as-fielded command-link posture (ArduRover defaults), so the test shows
# whether the out-of-the-box configuration is exploitable.
#
# Skid/twin-thruster output mapping (load-bearing for this hull's steering --
# ThrottleLeft/ThrottleRight, ArduRover's own skid-steer functions):
SERVO1_FUNCTION 73
SERVO3_FUNCTION 74
